;;;626    /**
;;;627      * @brief mask the specified I2C interrupt.
;;;628      * @param  I2Cx: where x can be 0 or 1
;;;629      * @param  I2C_INT
;;;630      * This parameter can be one of the following values:
;;;631      *     @arg I2C_INT_GEN_CALL: Set only when a General Call address is received and it is acknowledged.
;;;632      *     @arg I2C_INT_START_DET: Indicates whether a START or RESTART condition has occurred on the I2C
;;;633                                  interface regardless of whether I2C is operating in slave or master mode.
;;;634      *     @arg I2C_INT_STOP_DET:  Indicates whether a STOP condition has occurred on the I2C interface regardless
;;;635                                  of whether I2C is operating in slave or master mode
;;;636      *     @arg I2C_INT_ACTIVITY:  This bit captures I2C activity and stays set until it is cleared.
;;;637      *     @arg I2C_INT_RX_DONE:   When the I2C is acting as a slave-transmitter, this bit is set to 1 if the
;;;638                                  master does not acknowledge a transmitted byte. This occurs on the last byte of
